WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.641
A scheduler chooses among ready tasks.

00:00:02.641 --> 00:00:07.922
Different policies optimise different goals such as response time, throughput and fairness.

00:00:07.922 --> 00:00:15.404
Waiting time counts time spent ready but not running; turnaround time measures completion time minus arrival time.

00:00:15.404 --> 00:00:18.045
State all assumptions before comparing algorithms.

00:00:19.045 --> 00:00:22.965
A runs 0–4, B runs 4–6, C runs 6–9.

00:00:22.965 --> 00:00:26.886
Their waiting times are 0, 4 and 6 ms.

00:00:26.886 --> 00:00:30.371
Average waiting time is (0+4+6)/3 = 10/3 ms.

00:00:30.371 --> 00:00:33.420
No I/O or switching cost is assumed.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.319
For the original order, when does task C finish?

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:41.185
C begins at 6 ms and needs 3 ms of CPU time.
